* sg13g2-bandgap -- sg13cmos5l-startup-trip-point bench body for the
* `klt sim` harness (issue #337, Part of #322). Instantiated by
* sim/sg13cmos5l-startup-trip-point/run_klt_sim.sh, which substitutes
* @@OSDI_DIR@@. Source of every device line: the legacy sed-template
* tb_sg13cmos5l_startup_trip_point.spice.tmpl (still the generator of every
* committed record) -- same instance names, node names and W/L as
* design/sg13cmos5l/netlist/bandgap_startup.spice.
*
* `klt sim` netlist-body convention: this file is a circuit BODY. Moved out
* of the legacy template: the two `.lib` corner cards (cornerMOShv /
* cornerRES, now selected per process corner by the request), the
* `.options temp=T tnom=27` card (`klt sim` emits the corner's `.temp`),
* and the `op` / `dc` / `meas` control commands (now the request's
* `analysis` and `measurements`). No bipolar device here, so no PNP
* section is involved.
*
* Same one deliberate deviation as every `klt sim` body in this repo: the
* `.control` preload block below (klayout-tools#2666).
.control
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/mosvar.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/r3_cmc.osdi
.endc

* Rail. `klt sim` overrides this per corner via `alter Vvdd=<v>` from
* `corners.supply_v`.
Vvdd vdd 0 dc 3.30
Vvss vss 0 dc 0
* bandgap_startup.spice wires the rhigh bulk terminal to the global
* substrate net `sub!`; tied to vss through a 0 V source.
Vsub sub! vss dc 0

* FIXTURE 1 -- sns1 stimulus: stands in for the core's sense node so the
* startup circuit's response can be swept from "core is dead" (sns1 = 0) to
* "core is up" (sns1 = vdd). The request's dc analysis sweeps this source.
Vsns1 sns1 vss dc 0

* FIXTURE 2 -- fb load: 10 Mohm pull-up standing in for whatever eventually
* holds fb high, weak enough (<= 0.4 uA) not to contest XMKFB's pull-down.
Rfbpu vdd fb 10meg

XRPU vdd det sub! rhigh w=1u l=1411.3u m=1 b=0
XMSENSE det sns1 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1
XMKFB fb det vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=2u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1
